From 58187870ffff17b3ea5fcb5b480485f3f50ebbfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 01:19:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] provenance: a sha-pinned exemption ledger for the 15 commits
 --strict cannot pass without rewriting history

cmd_provenance consulted the sha-pinned ledger for the missing-Measured-effect class only (the 'elif not (is_native or sha in grandfathered)' arm); the loose-only arm had no ledger term at all. So the checklist's stated remedy - 'grandfather them explicitly with a reason' - was not executable for 12 of the 15 offenders, and the only other remedy was amending published, tagged, series-pinned commits.

trailer-exemptions.json is a NEW ledger, deliberately not native-grandfather.json (CLOSED by its own text) and not pending-trailers.json (debt owed by UNMERGED branches; these 15 are on arifi/main). Its 15 rows are derived from the tool's own predicates, not hand-listed.

An exemption is not a repair and the report must never let it read as one: a separate 'EXEMPT, NOT REPAIRED' counter, every exempted sha listed with its class, and a qualified PASS line. The unqualified 'PASS: every commit carries provenance.' is now unreachable whenever a row is in use, and the test asserts exactly that - plus that native-grandfather.json still does NOT clear a loose-only commit.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - audit tooling only; no inference code path is touched. provenance --strict over 658 commits: before rc=1 'FAIL (--strict): 12 loose-only, 3 without Measured-effect'; after rc=0 'PASS (15 EXEMPT, not repaired - 12 loose-only, 3 without Measured-effect)'. test_arifi_sync.py SeriesRegenTest 5 tests OK.
